//RS // Unix-domain streams and UDP sockets cannot be represented as `TcpStream`,
//RS // but they must park on the same task slots instead of blocking worker threads.
//RS // One process-wide poller owns all raw-descriptor readiness registrations.
//RS // The token is the logical handle identity. It carries the descriptor number,
//RS // not a cloned OS handle, so close/cancel share one lifecycle.
